WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
In a local-first pattern, requests go to a local model unless capability, capacity,

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.500
or availability requires an approved cloud alternative.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.650
This preserves local control for routine work.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.467
The fallback must check data classification before forwarding.

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:16.760
A sensitive request should fail safely or use a reduced local capability rather than cross

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.000
a prohibited boundary.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.500
A cloud-first pattern can keep preprocessing local.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.980
Private documents may be searched, filtered, summarized,

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.000
or redacted before an allowed subset is sent to a hosted model.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.565
Split retrieval and generation follows this idea:

00:00:28.565 --> 00:00:31.360
local systems retain source material and select passages,

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.000
while another environment generates the answer.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.680
Local embeddings can prevent raw documents from leaving,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.000
but retrieved text and vector metadata still require policy review.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.500
Cloud GPUs can handle heavy batch jobs or temporary models while daily inference remains

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:44.970
local.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:48.610
Edge inference places a model near sensors or users and sends only events, metrics,

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.000
or approved results to centralized coordination.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.580
A private assistant may expose a local default model and allow users to choose an external

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.070
model for approved tasks,

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:59.995
making the boundary visible instead of hiding it in automatic routing.

00:00:59.995 --> 00:01:04.580
Each pattern needs explicit interfaces, identities, logs, retention, timeouts,

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.000
and failure behavior.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Minimize data movement and shared state.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Begin with one justified split and test it end to end before adding routes.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.010
Patterns are not maturity levels;

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:18.000
the simplest one that satisfies the workload is usually the easiest to secure and recover.
